# Rover

- Canonical docs live under `docs/`: conceptual core, decisions log (`docs/decisions/README.md`), open decisions, consent, hardware, model. Start from `AGENTS.md`.
- Private material (applications, former vault notes, named people) lives in the private studio repo; never copy it here.
- Do not invent permissions, consent, corpus rights, or funding facts. No archive partnership exists yet.
- The fragments restrict the model by lookup and citation; never call them training data.
- Do not commit corpora, CAD/HTML chassis mockups, or large binaries unless an issue explicitly asks.
- Device name Fielding is fine; no literary homage until permission lands. Title: *Uncertain Field Notes*.
- Prefer *rover*, *device*, or *machine* over *instrument*. Write Newfoundland (Ktaqmkuk) on first mention.
- No phase dates in docs; dates live on issues.
- Dual license: CC BY 4.0 (docs), Apache-2.0 (software). See LICENSE.
- Prefer label `software` over `firmware`. Issue titles have no kind prefix.
- Avoid the word "master" in new user-facing text, docs, comments, and identifiers.
